course: dictionary
lesson: 11538
title: Taking turns with alternately
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alternately means first one thing, then another, again and again, taking turns. Think of a see-saw: one end goes up, then the other end goes up, and it keeps switching.
explain: In maths you might colour beads alternately: red, blue, red, blue. The word tells you the pattern switches each time, so you never get two reds in a row.
explain: In a story, «She was alternately laughing and crying» means she kept switching between laughing and crying. It does not mean she did both at the same time.
explain: Alternately is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. Look for the clue that the actions take turns.
fact: Alternately means first one thing, then another, again and again, taking turns.
fact: «Alternately» is an adverb: it tells you how something happens.
fact: «The two teams batted alternately» means one team batted, then the other, and so on.
fact: Alternately does not mean together. The two things take turns; they do not happen at the same moment.
fact: A similar phrase is «by turns», which also means one after another.
exercise: «Mia placed the beads alternately: red, then blue, then red again.» What does alternately mean here? | All at the same time | Very quickly and loudly | *Taking turns, one then the other | Without any colour
exercise: «The rain and the sun came alternately all afternoon.» What does alternately tell us? | *The rain and the sun took turns | The rain stopped for good | Only the sun came | The rain and the sun came together
exercise: Which word means the same idea as alternately? | *By turns | Suddenly | Together | Happily
test: «The dancers stepped alternately left and right.» Which one is closest in meaning? | *One step left, then one step right, again and again | Only left steps | Each step at the same time | Very slowly
test: «He was alternately cold and hot, so he kept taking his coat on and off.» Why did he take his coat on and off? | He liked to play with coats | *His body kept switching between cold and hot | He wanted to look smart | It was raining hard
exam: Ella wrote, «The lights flashed alternately green and red.» Which is true? | The lights stayed green all day | The lights never changed colour | The lights were green and red at the same time | *The lights changed between green and red, one after another
